{
  "comment": "DCE worker seccomp profile. STARTING PROFILE, to be validated in Phase 4 (SDD 9.8). Default action is deny (SCMP_ACT_ERRNO). The allowlist covers the syscalls CPython 3.12 and its common libraries need for file I/O, memory, threads, time, and exit. Network syscalls (socket, connect, bind, listen, accept, sendto, recvfrom) are intentionally absent: with --network none they are unnecessary and denying them is defence in depth. Namespace, mount, ptrace, bpf, and keyctl syscalls are absent. Clone is allowed because the PID limit (--pids-limit 64) is the bound that the fork-bomb test (T04) verifies, not seccomp. Validate every entry against the image on the Vultr VM.",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
  "architectures": [
    "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
    "SCMP_ARCH_X86",
    "SCMP_ARCH_AARCH64"
  ],
